{"id":"7a8b45d5-8b0e-44be-be11-b5d0ea4f62fd","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The 'args' parameter should be non-null during execution of 'main' as per Java runtime guarantees.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:54.971422Z"}
{"id":"c49a4a12-09f0-4443-ae49-fe962090d229","expr":"b == 0 ? result == Integer.MIN_VALUE : result == a / b","rationale":"Captures the method's documented behavior: if b is 0, returns MIN_VALUE, else returns integer division.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:54.971840Z"}
{"id":"b09d5cd8-fac4-43b6-ac0c-e8c5e86dbf42","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The 'args' parameter, supplied by the JVM to main, is never null in standard usage.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:54.971822Z"}
{"id":"94e9d859-0d38-412e-8e86-42bfd5ad842e","expr":"b == 0 || a / b * b + a % b == a","rationale":"If b == 0, division is not performed; otherwise, basic property of integer division and modulus ensures this holds.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:54.971677Z"}
{"id":"08ce4dca-e0dc-46cf-83c7-3de875833d1d","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"All arrays in Java have a non-negative length.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:54.971822Z"}
{"id":"09f59ec6-94bc-405b-a5f6-861dcfa18511","expr":"b == 0 || result == a / b","rationale":"If b is not zero, result is exactly a / b.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:54.971840Z"}
{"id":"dd476650-6e68-4399-addf-c11cc9015190","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"The length of an array in Java is always non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:54.971422Z"}
{"id":"21aa6ca8-96b2-4ca5-98d9-0ed45cafd0aa","expr":"b == 0 || b * result <= a && a < b * (result + 1)","rationale":"If b != 0, result is integer division so this gives the mathematical bounds for a in integer division.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:54.971840Z"}
{"id":"d496893b-b241-460a-a4a6-174ec9a76098","expr":"args.getClass().isArray()","rationale":"The 'args' variable is always a Java array.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:54.971822Z"}
{"id":"d8e169a1-2eaf-43e7-b126-1a0cdbe38c62","expr":"b != 0 || Integer.MIN_VALUE == Integer.MIN_VALUE","rationale":"If b is 0, the method returns Integer.MIN_VALUE, so this invariant is trivially always true but conveys method's documented behavior.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:54.971677Z"}
{"id":"44c5a7f9-7b35-42e5-bc24-bc0283b2f981","expr":"b != 0 || result == Integer.MIN_VALUE","rationale":"If b is zero, result must be Integer.MIN_VALUE.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:54.971840Z"}
{"id":"296661d7-4770-44e5-bc77-453983a120fa","expr":"(b > 0) || (b <= 0)","rationale":"This covers all integer possibilities for b, and is useful as a partitioning fact.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:54.971677Z"}
{"id":"2cfb9a0e-e462-4d8f-aaaf-2a1a82d15ddd","expr":"b == 0 || Math.abs(result) <= Math.abs(a)","rationale":"If b != 0, division reduces the magnitude or keeps it the same.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:54.971840Z"}
{"id":"ac848634-9719-4a79-8a3d-3ea09eebb124","expr":"a == 0 || a != 0","rationale":"This partitions the input space regarding 'a'; while tautological, it helps coverage analysis.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:54.971677Z"}
